  <h1>About Dispatch Cove</h1>
  <p class="dek">A small desk for truck dispatchers and owner-operators in the United States. The promise is a clear answer to a real job, not a pile of products.</p>
  <p>Dispatch Cove is operated by Etern Digital. The site publishes practical guides on <a href="/getting-started/">getting started in dispatch</a>, <a href="/load-boards/">load boards</a>, <a href="/factoring/">freight factoring</a>, <a href="/software/">dispatch software</a>, and issues that matter to <a href="/owner-operators/">owner-operators</a>. The writing is in American English, for people who book freight or run trucks in the United States.</p>
  <h2>How a guide gets written</h2>
  <p>We start with the task. Published examples are <a href="/getting-started/how-to-become-a-truck-dispatcher-with-no-experience/">how to become a truck dispatcher with no experience</a>, <a href="/load-boards/dat-vs-truckstop-for-a-new-dispatcher/">DAT vs Truckstop for a new dispatcher</a>, and <a href="/factoring/freight-factoring-recourse-vs-non-recourse/">recourse vs non-recourse freight factoring</a>. We say what the job needs, what it does not need, and where a product is only one option. Official requirements are linked to the agency or the company that published them. We do not invent tests, statistics, or testimonials.</p>
  <p>Guides are general information. They are not legal, tax, insurance, or financial advice, and they are not a substitute for FMCSA rules, a written contract, or a licensed professional. An insurance checklist, when we publish one, is an explainer of documents people commonly review, not a recommendation to buy or skip a policy.</p>
  <h2>How the site is paid for</h2>
  <p>Some links are affiliate links. If you buy through one, we may earn a commission, and the price you pay is the seller’s price. Those links use <code>rel="sponsored"</code>. A short note sits just before the first offer link in a guide, and the footer also carries the disclosure. Some offer boxes still wait on an approved affiliate URL; those boxes are marked and do not contain a live offer link.</p>
  <p>The full terms are on the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>. Questions about an account, a refund, or a funded invoice belong to the company that took the agreement. We do not have those records.</p>
  <h2>Write to us</h2>
  <p>Corrections are welcome. If a sentence is wrong, say so. Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>, or use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
